    2. JSON & JSON PATH 
        1. Some comparison between YAML and JSON 
            1.1 JSON is also used for storing data just like YAML and it is different from YAML, especially with it's syntax.
            1.2 YAML uses Indendations to seperate each item in the list meanwhile JSON uses commas.
            1.3 In YAML list/array is denoted with "-" at the beginning of each item while JSON uses "[ ]".
            1.4 YAML uses indentation for dictionaries while JSON uses curly brackets.
        2. JSONPATH is the query language for JSON
            2.1 After storing data in json files we will retrieve them. And for that we need to have a standardized way of doing that, a query language.
            2.2 If the top level dictionary does not have a name, then it is denoted by the "$" sign.
            2.3 Dictionaries within dictionaries are denoted by ".". Like $.vehicles.model
            2.4 Items inside arrays are denoted by "[]". The second item is shown as model[1]
            2.5 We can write conditions for our query, model[? ( @>40 ) ] or [? ( @.location == "rear-right")].model
                I. @ is used to express "for each item"
